    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35171" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-longus</span></b> , a, um, adj.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>very long.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">via,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 5, 20, 8</span></i>
			: perlongum. adverb., <i>for a very long
			time</i>, <i>very long</i>, 
			
			<i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr. 1,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>very tedious</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 3, 3, 17</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perlongē</span></b> , <i>a very long way
			off</i>, <i>very far</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perlonge est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 3, 5, 61</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
